  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Probate",
   "links": [],
   "region": "main"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "A Probate is a court supervised process for identifying and gathering assets of a deceased person.",
   "links": [],
   "region": "main"
  },
  {
   "type": "ul",
   "items": [
    {
     "text": "The Process of winding down a decedents affairs",
     "links": [],
     "children": []
    },
    {
     "text": "Appointment of a personal representative",
     "links": [],
     "children": []
    },
    {
     "text": "Determination of validity of will",
     "links": [],
     "children": []
    },
    {
     "text": "Paying claims",
     "links": [],
     "children": []
    },
    {
     "text": "Distributing assets",
     "links": [],
     "children": []
    },
    {
     "text": "Filing necessary tax returns",
     "links": [],
     "children": []
    }
   ],
   "region": "main"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "It is important to know that having a will does not avoid Probate. If you want to avoid Probate you will need a trust based estate plan. Contact Vaughn Law for a consultation to discuss this further.",
   "links": [],
   "region": "main"
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Summary Administration vs. Final Administration",
   "links": [],
   "region": "main"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "There are different types of Probate Administration in Florida.",
   "links": [],
   "region": "main"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Formal Administration is the traditional procedure for winding down a decedent’s affairs. This procedure can be used with any Probate regardless of assets but is a lengthy process that requires proper notice to be provided to those creditors who are known or unknown to the estate.",
   "links": [],
   "region": "main"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Summary Administration is an expedited process to wind down a decedent’s affairs for small estates.",
   "links": [],
   "region": "main"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "To qualify for a Summary Administration the following must be true:",
   "links": [],
   "region": "main"
  },
  {
   "type": "ul",
   "items": [
    {
     "text": "Less than $75,000, and",
     "links": [],
     "children": []
    },
    {
     "text": "Dead more than two years",
     "links": [],
     "children": []
    },
    {
     "text": "Or if the decedent only owned a homestead property, regardless of value",
     "links": [],
     "children": []
    }
   ],
   "region": "main"
  },
  {
